.\" OpenBSD-style concise man page
.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt ID 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm id
.Nd print real and effective user and group IDs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm id
.Op Fl GgunrzV
.Op Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility prints user and group information for the specified
.Ar user ,
or for the current user if no
.Ar user
is specified.
.Pp
The default output shows the effective user ID, group ID, and all
group memberships in the format:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
uid=N(name) gid=N(name) groups=N(name),N(name),...
.Ed
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl g , Fl Fl group
Print only the effective group ID.
.It Fl G , Fl Fl groups
Print all group IDs.
.It Fl h , Fl Fl help
Display a help message and exit.
.It Fl n , Fl Fl name
Print the name instead of the numeric ID.
Must be used with
.Fl g ,
.Fl G ,
or
.Fl u .
.It Fl r , Fl Fl real
Print the real ID instead of the effective ID.
Must be used with
.Fl g ,
.Fl G ,
or
.Fl u .
.It Fl u , Fl Fl user
Print only the effective user ID.
.It Fl V , Fl Fl version
Output version information and exit.
.It Fl z , Fl Fl zero
Delimit entries with NUL characters instead of whitespace.
.El
.Pp
The
.Fl u ,
.Fl g ,
and
.Fl G
options are mutually exclusive.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std id
.Sh EXAMPLES
Print full identity information:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ id
uid=1000(alice) gid=1000(alice) groups=1000(alice),27(sudo)
.Ed
.Pp
Print only the effective user name:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ id -un
alice
.Ed
.Pp
Print all group names for a specific user:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ id -Gn root
root
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr groups 1 ,
.Xr logname 1 ,
.Xr whoami 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is compliant with the
.St -p1003.1-2008
specification.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An "vibeutils implementation by Travis Cole"
